t-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the latest deploy (v2.3.1), with an error rate of 18% in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The SRE agent rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release (v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 were both unhealthy). After the rollback the service is healthy in all regions at v2.3.0, with an error rate of 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 56704, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GgGiDfzkaQuf9Q678sHtiV", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56704, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GgGiDfzkaQuf9Q678sHtiV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 61620, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **The problem:** Version v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The deploy list isn't in date order, so I went by release sequence. The two releases after v2.3.0, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were both unhealthy, so I skipped them.\n- **After the rollback:** All three regions are on v2.3.0 and pass health checks, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** It describes the failure, the rollback and the result. It also 