 The SRE agent rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release (v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 were both unhealthy). After the rollback the service is healthy in all regions at v2.3.0, with an error rate of 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **The problem:** Version v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The deploy list isn't in date order, so I went by release sequence. The two releases after v2.3.0, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were both unhealthy, so I skipped them.\n- **After the rollback:** All three regions are on v2.3.0 and pass health checks, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** It describes the failure, the rollback and the result. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 problem needs to be found before anyone redeploys it. There were no open incidents beforehand, so it doesn't duplicate an existing one.", "type": "text"}]}]}